1
00:00:00,132 --> 00:00:01,832
Or, uh, Ticket to Ride?

2
00:00:01,834 --> 00:00:02,934
Hearthstone?

3
00:00:02,935 --> 00:00:07,735
I... what would you be
the happiest losing at?

4
00:00:09,541 --> 00:00:11,371
(Penny:)I don't want to
play a game, Sheldon.

5
00:00:11,377 --> 00:00:16,317
(Sheldon:)Wow, and I remember when you
loved playing games with me.

6
00:00:16,315 --> 00:00:19,115
(Sheldon:)Maybe Penny isn't the only
relationship you're phoning in.

7
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,350
It's not that I'd
stopped trying,

8
00:00:23,355 --> 00:00:26,355
it's just how
relationships progress.

9
00:00:26,358 --> 00:00:28,258
(Leonard:)They start with infatuation,

10
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:31,760
(Leonard:)but over time mellow into
something more comfortable.

11
00:00:31,764 --> 00:00:33,864
(Sheldon:)Hmm. Yeah, you're right.

12
00:00:33,866 --> 00:00:35,466
(Sheldon:)It's like when
I first encountered

13
00:00:35,467 --> 00:00:37,037
(Sheldon:)the Pythagorean Theorem.

14
00:00:37,036 --> 00:00:38,506
(Leonard:)You know,
I was blown away

15
00:00:38,504 --> 00:00:40,504
(Sheldon:)that the square
of the hypotenuse

16
00:00:40,506 --> 00:00:43,336
(Sheldon:)was the sum of the squares
of the opposite sides.

17
00:00:43,342 --> 00:00:46,042
Yeah, but now
I'm just like "eh."

18
00:00:49,748 --> 00:00:53,048
(Howard:)Okay, this grid
represents the room.

19
00:00:53,052 --> 00:00:57,222
(Howard:)All we need to do is plot out
where each squeak is

20
00:00:57,222 --> 00:01:02,022
(Howard:)and we can find a quiet
path to the crib.

